title    Basie Street Shout
composer Claude
about    A three-chorus Bb blues shout for big band: brass call and sax answer, then a sax soli over brass backgrounds, then a full tutti shout and a 6/9 button.
tempo    176
beats    4
steps    2       # eighth-note grid, 8 steps per bar
swing    0.3     # close to a triplet swing feel at this medium-up tempo

# Form: 12-bar jazz blues in Bb, three choruses plus a two-bar tag.
# | Bb7 | Eb7 | Bb7 | Fm7 Bb7 | Eb7 | Edim7 | Bb7 | G7b9 | Cm7 | F7 | Bb7 G7 | Cm7 F7 |
# All pitches are concert pitch.
#
# Section-writing plan:
# - Each section is one or more voices playing explicit note stacks.
# - Trumpets: always 4-way close under the lead (span within an octave), so the section reads as one bright block.
#   The lead stays between Bb5 and D6 most of the time and only reaches F6 (written G6) at the climaxes.
# - Saxes: lead alto plus three voices in 4-way close (alto 2, tenor 1, tenor 2), and the bari doubles the lead
#   an octave below in the soli passages (the classic "5-way, doubled lead" sound). In the tutti shout the altos and
#   tenors double the trumpet voicing an octave down and the bari moves to roots with the bass trombone.
# - Trombones: open, spread voicings (root low, guide tones 3 and 7 in the middle, a colour tone on top) that sit
#   under the saxes and never cross above the trumpets' bottom note.
# - Passing notes in the sax lines are harmonized with diminished-seventh chords (the dim7 is the standard
#   way to keep 4-way close moving in parallel through non-chord tones).

# Saxes: alto pair (lead + 2nd), tenor pair, bari. Panned left, as on a bandstand front row.
voice alto  altosax  vol=0.72 pan=-0.30 gate=0.92
voice tenor tenorsax vol=0.72 pan=-0.45 gate=0.92
voice bari  barisax  vol=0.80 pan=-0.55 gate=0.92
# Brass: four trumpets in one voice, four trombones in one voice. Trumpets slightly right, trombones further right.
voice tpt   trumpet  vol=0.68 pan=0.25 gate=0.9
voice tbn   trombone vol=0.74 pan=0.50 gate=0.92
# Rhythm section: Basie-style sparse piano, walking upright bass, and a swinging kit.
voice piano piano    vol=0.50 pan=0.60 gate=0.45
voice bass  upright  vol=0.95
voice ride  ride     vol=0.45
voice hat   hat      vol=0.40
voice kick  kick     vol=0.45
voice snare snare    vol=0.55
voice crash crash    vol=0.50

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Chorus A: call and response between brass and saxes.
# - Brass (tpt + tbn together) state a one-bar riff in bars 1, 3, 5, 7: a quarter hit on beat 1,
#   a short "and of 2", and an accented quarter on 4. Trumpets voice it Bb7 in close position with the
#   3rd on top (D6 Bb5 Ab5 F5); trombones add root, 7th, 3rd, and 13th underneath (Bb2 Ab3 D4 G4).
#   Bar 5 moves the same shape to Eb7 with Db6 on top so the riff follows the IV chord.
# - Saxes answer in bars 2, 4, 6, 8 with harmonized eighth-note lines in 4-way close and the bari on the
#   lead an octave down. Bar 6 is a straight Edim7 climb (every chord is an inversion of the same dim7).
# - Bars 9-12 overlap the sections: the brass hold long chords and short pushes while the saxes run a
#   continuous harmonized line underneath, so the turnaround drives into chorus B.
# - Piano comps only on offbeats (beats 2-and and 4) in a rootless mid-register voicing so it never
#   competes with the horn stacks. Ride, hat on 2 and 4, feathered kick, light ghosted snare.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pattern chorusA
tpt   | D6+Bb5+Ab5+F5-! . C6+Ab5+F5+D5 .- D6+Bb5+Ab5+F5-! | _ | D6+Bb5+Ab5+F5-! . C6+Ab5+F5+D5 .- D6+Bb5+Ab5+F5-! | _ |
tpt   | Db6+Bb5+G5+F5-! . C6+G5+F5+Db5 .- Db6+Bb5+G5+F5-! | _ | D6+Bb5+Ab5+F5-! . C6+Ab5+F5+D5 .- D6+Bb5+Ab5+F5-! | _ |
tpt   | . D6+Bb5+G5+Eb5------ | -- . C6+A5+G5+Eb5-! .-- | D6+Bb5+Ab5+F5- . D6+Bb5+Ab5+F5 B5+Ab5+F5+D5--- | Bb5+G5+Eb5+D5- .- C6+A5+G5+Eb5-! .- |
tbn   | Bb2+Ab3+D4+G4-! . Bb2+Ab3+D4+G4 .- Bb2+Ab3+D4+G4-! | _ | Bb2+Ab3+D4+G4-! . Bb2+Ab3+D4+G4 .- Bb2+Ab3+D4+G4-! | _ |
tbn   | Eb3+Bb3+Db4+G4-! . Eb3+Bb3+Db4+G4 .- Eb3+Bb3+Db4+G4-! | _ | Bb2+Ab3+D4+G4-! . Bb2+Ab3+D4+G4 .- Bb2+Ab3+D4+G4-! | _ |
tbn   | . C3+G3+Bb3+Eb4------ | -- . F2+Eb3+A3+D4-! .-- | Bb2+Ab3+D4+G4- . Bb2+Ab3+D4+G4 G2+F3+B3+D4--- | C3+G3+Bb3+Eb4- .- F2+Eb3+A3+D4-! .- |
alto  | _ | . Bb4+G4 Db5+Bb4 C5+G4- Bb4+G4 G4+Eb4- | _ | . Ab4+F4 C5+Ab4 Eb5+C5 D5+Bb4- Bb4+Ab4 Ab4+F4 |
alto  | _ | . G4+E4 Bb4+G4 Db5+Bb4 E5+Db5- Db5+Bb4 Bb4+G4 | _ | . B4+Ab4 D5+B4 F5+D5- Eb5+B4 D5+B4 B4+Ab4 |
alto  | G4+Eb4- Bb4+G4 C5+Bb4 D5+Bb4 Eb5+C5 D5+Bb4 C5+Bb4 | A4+F4- C5+A4 Eb5+C5 D5+A4 C5+A4 A4+F4 F4+Eb4 | Bb4+Ab4- Ab4+F4 F4+D4 B4+Ab4- D5+B4 F5+D5 | Eb5+C5- D5+Bb4 C5+Bb4 A4+F4- C5+A4 Eb5+C5 |
tenor | _ | . Eb4+Db4 G4+Eb4 Eb4+Db4- Eb4+Db4 Db4+Bb3- | _ | . Eb4+C4 F4+Eb4 Ab4+F4 Ab4+F4- F4+D4 D4+C4 |
tenor | _ | . Db4+Bb3 E4+Db4 G4+E4 Bb4+G4- G4+E4 E4+Db4 | _ | . F4+D4 Ab4+F4 B4+Ab4- G4+F4 Ab4+F4 F4+D4 |
tenor | C4+Bb3- Eb4+C4 G4+Eb4 G4+Eb4 Bb4+G4 G4+Eb4 G4+Eb4 | Eb4+C4- F4+Eb4 A4+F4 G4+Eb4 F4+Eb4 Eb4+C4 C4+A3 | F4+D4- D4+C4 C4+Ab3 F4+D4- Ab4+F4 B4+Ab4 | Bb4+G4- G4+Eb4 G4+Eb4 Eb4+C4- F4+Eb4 A4+F4 |
bari  | _ | . Bb3 Db4 C4- Bb3 G3- | _ | . Ab3 C4 Eb4 D4- Bb3 Ab3 |
bari  | _ | . G3 Bb3 Db4 E4- Db4 Bb3 | _ | . B3 D4 F4- Eb4 D4 B3 |
bari  | G3- Bb3 C4 D4 Eb4 D4 C4 | A3- C4 Eb4 D4 C4 A3 F3 | Bb3- Ab3 F3 B3- D4 F4 | Eb4- D4 C4 A3- C4 Eb4 |
piano | .-- Ab3+C4+D4+G4 . . Ab3+C4+D4+G4 . | .-- G3+C4+Db4+F4 . . G3+C4+Db4+F4 . | .-- Ab3+C4+D4+G4 . . Ab3+C4+D4+G4 . | . Ab3+C4+Eb4+G4 .- . Ab3+C4+D4+G4 .- |
piano | .-- G3+C4+Db4+F4 . . G3+C4+Db4+F4 . | .-- G3+Bb3+Db4+E4 . . G3+Bb3+Db4+E4 . | .-- Ab3+C4+D4+G4 . . Ab3+C4+D4+G4 . | .-- F3+Ab3+B3+D4 . . F3+Ab3+B3+D4 . |
piano | .-- Bb3+D4+Eb4+G4 . . Bb3+D4+Eb4+G4 . | .-- Eb3+G3+A3+D4 . . Eb3+G3+A3+D4 . | . Ab3+C4+D4+G4 .- . F3+Ab3+B3+D4 .- | . Bb3+D4+Eb4+G4 .- . Eb3+G3+A3+D4 .- |
bass  | Bb1- D2- F2- E2- | Eb2- F2- G2- A2- | Bb2- Ab2- F2- D2- | F2- Ab2- Bb2- D2- |
bass  | Eb2- G2- Bb2- G2- | E2- G2- Bb2- Db3- | D3- C3- Bb2- Ab2- | G2- B2- D3- Db3- |
bass  | C3- Bb2- G2- Eb2- | F2- Eb2- C2- A1- | Bb1- D2- G1- B1- | C2- Eb2- F2- A1- |
ride  | x.xx x.xx | x.xx x.xx | x.xx x.xx | x.xx x.xx | x.xx x.xx | x.xx x.xx |
ride  | x.xx x.xx | x.xx x.xx | x.xx x.xx | x.xx x.xx | x.xx x.xx | x.xx x.xx |
hat   | ..x. ..x. | ..x. ..x. | ..x. ..x. | ..x. ..x. | ..x. ..x. | ..x. ..x. |
hat   | ..x. ..x. | ..x. ..x. | ..x. ..x. | ..x. ..x. | ..x. ..x. | ..x. ..x. |
kick  | o.o. o.o. | o.o. o.o. | o.o. o.o. | o.o. o.o. | o.o. o.o. | o.o. o.o. |
kick  | o.o. o.o. | o.o. o.o. | o.o. o.o. | o.o. o.o. | o.o. o.o. | o.o. o.o. |
snare | .... ..o. | .... ..o. | .... ..o. | .... ..o. | .... ..o. | .... ..o. |
snare | .... ..o. | .... ..o. | .... ..o. | .... ..o. | .... ..o. | .... o.x. |
crash | x... .... | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ |
crash | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Chorus B: the roles flip. Saxes carry the melody as a soli; brass becomes the background.
# - Saxes: a 12-bar swinging line in 4-way close with the bari doubling the lead an octave below.
#   The phrases leave holes (bars 2, 4, 6, 7, 9, 11, 12) on purpose.
# - Trumpets only punch into those holes with short close-voiced stabs, so the two sections interlock
#   instead of stacking. Bar 7's A natural in the sax line is harmonized as a dim7 (D7b9 sound) leading to G7.
# - Trombones play soft sustained pads ("?" dynamics) entering on beat 2 of each phrase, voiced low
#   (top note at or below Eb4) so they sit under the saxes like a cushion and move by guide tones
#   (Ab3 to G3, D4 to Db4) from chord to chord.
# - Bar 12: the trombones crescendo on F7 and the trumpets play a two-note pickup into the shout,
#   while the snare fills.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pattern chorusB
alto  | . D5+Bb4 F5+D5 D5+Bb4 Db5+Bb4 C5+Ab4 Bb4+Ab4- | Db5+Bb4- C5+G4 Bb4+G4- .-- | . F4+D4 G4+D4 Ab4+F4 Bb4+Ab4 C5+Ab4 D5+Bb4 F5+D5 | Eb5+C5- C5+Ab4 Ab4+F4 D5+Bb4- .- |
alto  | G5+Eb5- F5+Db5 Eb5+Db5 Db5+Bb4 C5+G4 Bb4+G4 G4+Eb4 | E4+Db4- G4+E4 Bb4+G4 Db5+Bb4- .- | D5+Bb4- . Bb4+Ab4 .- Ab4+F4 A4+F#4 | B4+Ab4- . D5+B4 F5+D5- Eb5+B4 D5+B4 |
alto  | Eb5+C5--- D5+Bb4 C5+Bb4 Bb4+G4 G4+Eb4 | A4+F4- C5+A4 Eb5+C5- D5+A4 C5+A4 A4+F4 | Bb4+Ab4--- B4+Ab4- D5+B4 F5+D5 | Eb5+C5- . C5+Bb4 A4+F4- .- |
tenor | . Ab4+F4 Bb4+Ab4 Ab4+F4 G4+E4 F4+D4 F4+D4- | G4+Eb4- Eb4+Db4 Eb4+Db4- .-- | . Bb3+Ab3 C4+Ab3 D4+Bb3 F4+D4 F4+D4 Ab4+F4 Bb4+Ab4 | Ab4+F4- F4+Eb4 Eb4+C4 Ab4+F4- .- |
tenor | Db5+Bb4- Bb4+G4 Bb4+G4 G4+Eb4 Eb4+Db4 Eb4+Db4 Db4+Bb3 | Bb3+G3- Db4+Bb3 E4+Db4 G4+E4- .- | Ab4+F4- . F4+D4 .- D4+Bb3 Eb4+C4 | F4+D4- . Ab4+F4 B4+Ab4- G4+F4 Ab4+F4 |
tenor | Bb4+G4--- G4+Eb4 G4+Eb4 Eb4+C4 C4+Bb3 | Eb4+C4- F4+Eb4 A4+F4- G4+Eb4 F4+Eb4 Eb4+C4 | F4+D4--- F4+D4- Ab4+F4 B4+Ab4 | Bb4+G4- . G4+Eb4 Eb4+C4- .- |
bari  | . D4 F4 D4 Db4 C4 Bb3- | Db4- C4 Bb3- .-- | . F3 G3 Ab3 Bb3 C4 D4 F4 | Eb4- C4 Ab3 D4- .- |
bari  | G4- F4 Eb4 Db4 C4 Bb3 G3 | E3- G3 Bb3 Db4- .- | D4- . Bb3 .- Ab3 A3 | B3- . D4 F4- Eb4 D4 |
bari  | Eb4--- D4 C4 Bb3 G3 | A3- C4 Eb4- D4 C4 A3 | Bb3--- B3- D4 F4 | Eb4- . C4 A3- .- |
tpt   | _ | .---- Db6+Bb5+G5+F5 Db6+Bb5+G5+F5-! | _ | .----- D6+Bb5+Ab5+F5-! |
